# Reports are regenerable via dvc repro and stay out of git — except figure
# specs, which are committed as deployable artifacts (see deploy/DEPLOY.md).
# The RAG retrieval index (data/index/) is the opt-in exception: enable chat
# by running `dvc repro` in this project on the host.
/reports/*
!/reports/figures/
/reports/*.json
/reports/*.html
# …except the runtime-served summary files (the API serves both at
# /projects/01-rag-agent/{metrics,report}) — same rationale as DEPLOY.md.
!/reports/metrics.json
!/reports/report.html
# …and the retrieval-arm comparison the evaluation section cites — every
# public number traces to a committed artifact.
!/reports/fusion.json
# …and the expanded sealed set's retrieval-side read + failure taxonomy
# (Project A); the generation-side numbers land in metrics.json detail.
!/reports/sealed_retrieval.json
# …and the generation pass's per-question traces (55 sealed answers; same
# evidence role as the committed tuning traces).
!/reports/question_traces_heldout.json
# …and the citation pass's claim-level records (per-claim verify evidence).
!/reports/citation_records_heldout.json
# …and the stress pass's per-question traces (same evidence role).
!/reports/question_traces_stress.json
# …and the R6 sealed re-run + independent set B traces (same evidence role).
!/reports/question_traces_stress_after_r6.json
!/reports/question_traces_stress_b.json
# …and the R6 failure ledger (trace review required before interventions).
!/reports/stress_failure_ledger.md
/reports/figures/*.html
# The sealed held-out golden set is authored source data (like
# src/rag_agent/eval_questions.json), not a regenerable artifact: track it even
# though the repo-wide `data/` ignore (DVC) covers everything else under here.
!data/
data/*
!data/golden_heldout.json
!data/golden_stress.json
# …and the R6 independent stress set B (authored + sealed before any R6
# tuning, like the other sealed sets).
!data/golden_stress_b.json
